  "checks": [
    "Original A actually submits a checked Gather plus Store, retires, detaches, returns its original writers and publishes true bounded ready guards. A warm B imported transaction owns zero source leases and the real independent destinations.",
    "Warm B binds complete Store-ready guards authenticated against original ticket root, generation, slot coordinates and precise range. The original F32 indexed GDN route6/implementation7 or conv route7/implementation8 is one selected region with native dispatch_count=1.",
    "B genuinely records and executes the first ready capture. After real retirement, imported take returns only destination writers; release_outputs withdraws the exact source bundle while retaining only the dormant physical capture tuple. No whole-Invocation reset or arbitrary ready projection is used.",
    "A next generation of submission rewrites the same physical source slots and original private ID carrier. B rebinds the empty-ready pending Source and independent original destinations, then reuses the existing capture with recorded_capture_range_count=0 and reused_capture_range_count=1.",
    "The same-ID path retains the actual successful metadata carrier and skips mutation/upload/wait only when complete fixed geometry and values match. Both real host gates complete without timing out; changed IDs retain the original native upload/guard checks. This is a finite contract check, not a measured latency claim.",
    "The actual B dependency reports source_count=1, device_wait_count=1 and host_wait_count=0; ordinary submit is rejected. A truly retires and publishes its original destination while B remains gate-pending, and publication does not reopen writes.",
    "GDN B2/T4/K1/H2/S16 and conv B2/T1/K1/L3/C128 use noncontiguous source slots [1,5], destination slots [3,7], real capacity P8 and padded strides. Original dense public operations provide the mathematical reference; output/state match bitwise and whole-bank sentinel, old snapshots and padding remain exact.",
    "A real checked-Gather out-of-range failure remains the complete predecessor verdict: Store publication returns the same error, B receives that error and exposes no activation. After actual B retirement and Completion release, imported destinations can be taken and the failed source bundle can be released without publishing failed state."
  ],
  "interface_negatives": [
    "A complete same-count/same-length ready array with one genuine untouched but wrong-root/slot guard is InvalidArgument; the authentic complete array then binds and executes normally.",
    "Retired warm B cannot release its source bundle before taking the nominated writers; the subsequent real take and release succeed, proving refusal did not partially withdraw it.",
    "B pending behind its actual gate cannot release the source bundle; its later success or full failure verdict and cleanup remain intact.",
    "The checked-failure case returns the real imported writers and successfully releases only after actual retirement; it never publishes failed B state."
  ],
